  "details": "1. Add a VRC Scale Constraints to ObjectA on AvatarA.\n\n2. Lock Constraints setting, check Freeze To World in Advanced Settings.\n\n3. Upload AvatarA.\n\n4. Use AvatarA and change its avatar height in menu.\n\n5. Change to other avatar.\n\n6. Change to AvatarA.\n\n7. Now the scale of AvatarA's ObjectA is different on local and remote side. The scale is froze as 1,1,1 on local as expected behavior,  but the scale is froze as the avatar's height setting on the remote side.\n\nFeel like the initialization of VRC Constraints Freeze To World is slower than avatar height scaling on remote side? And it used avatar height scaling to freeze?\n\nThis problem doesn't exist on VRC Scale Constraints while using the old fashion way, an world origin prefab instead of Freeze To World. Both local and remote are remains 1,1,1.",
